{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 48, :comments ["<b>And he gathered all the food.</b> This is the fifth part that he gathered from the fields. <b>And he laid up food in the cities.</b> The fact that he mentioned 'all food' indicates that he gathered everything eaten by man — grain and bread and provisions, even figs and raisins and the like. <b>The food of the field that was round about it he laid up within it.</b> From here our Rabbis of blessed memory learned that the very soil of the place preserves the grain of that place."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 41, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:19:36.171273236Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}